I have updated NaaradControlFragment.kt so that the Controls panel
updates its theme reactively when you change theme settings in the
Settings tab: Cause & Fix (NaaradControlFragment.kt)

Cause: Previously, themeModeState and dynamicColorState were
non-reactive local variables initialized only once in
onCreateView(). Because onCreateView() is not re-invoked when
switching between tabs in ViewPager2, NaaradControlFragment never
recomposed when theme preferences changed.

Fix:

i. Converted themeModeState and dynamicColorState to reactive Compose
   state fields (mutableIntStateOf and mutableStateOf):

     private var themeModeState by mutableIntStateOf(0)
     private var dynamicColorState by mutableStateOf(true)

ii. Updated onResume() to refresh themeModeState and dynamicColorState
    from preferences whenever returning to the Controls tab:

      override fun onResume() {
        super.onResume()
        themeModeState = getPreference("themeMode", 0)
        dynamicColorState = getPreference("dynamicColorEnabled", true)
        controlViewModel.lastJsonData?.let { json -> setSensorValues(json) }
      }

Changing the Theme Mode (System Default, Light, Dark) or Dynamic Color
settings in the Settings tab now updates the Controls panel theme and
colors instantly.

